      "id": "v38-1y79l",
      "text": "An internet urban legend claims thieves are using drug-filled perfume bottles to render victims unconscious and rob them, a claim that has persisted since 2000. The drug mentioned in the rumor, \"Axter,\" is believed to refer to hydroxyzine, an antihistamine that can cause drowsiness and dizziness, but there is no evidence to support the claim that it can render someone unconscious as described. The claim, which has evolved over time, is considered a copypasta and has been debunked by fact-checkers, with no reputable news outlets reporting any instances of these attacks occurring. Claim:",
